<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:34Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>As Gambia gears up for election, can Barrow secure a third term?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c7e999763e2da055840e72cdcacb2269b0ff4088a8ea79636b5b86518c26965</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-gambia-gears-up-for-election-can-barrow-secure-a-third-term/a-80076340--b6856a8ea5b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-gambia-gears-up-for-election-can-barrow-secure-a-third-term/a-80076340?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Adama Barrow is seeking a third term as Gambians vote on December 5. The election will test the opposition's appeal and the country's progress on democratic reform.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Guinea-Bissau junta delays presidential vote for 2 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a86da4b5d7b37a4818ebe20c42e225616b61514583d8eef30fe0f5bdaa893715</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T20:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/guinea-bissau-junta-delays-presidential-vote-for-2-years/a-80068910--e34f489a3b6d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/guinea-bissau-junta-delays-presidential-vote-for-2-years/a-80068910?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The decision came exactly one year after the military took power on November 26, 2025. The junta said the conditions were insufficient to hold presidential elections for now.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's opposition voices face growing pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a38d561c7e01d65a75b716a28c86cd17504d0ee4e64e0dd3892b653f24c3c911</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-opposition-voices-face-growing-pressure/a-80063893--fc3fb0c33bdb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-opposition-voices-face-growing-pressure/a-80063893?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Opposition politicians and government critics say arrests, prosecutions and restrictions on public activity are making it harder to challenge those in power. Is a broader pattern emerging?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia-Ukraine war extends to the Baltic and the Mediterranean</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01b6c9796b5fc912dca17e7f60d88fac4c8963b829621bffc96f3612625278d2</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T09:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-ukraine-war-extends-to-the-baltic-and-the-mediterranean/a-80054604--5dcdff651bad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-ukraine-war-extends-to-the-baltic-and-the-mediterranean/a-80054604?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">By attacking Russian vessels around the world, Ukraine is trying to increase the pressure on Russia and also sending out signals to its Western allies. What is the impact on global maritime trade?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Egypt: At least 31 dead after fuel truck overturns on highway</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e45ed5ba8605599773e0d436691b30482df6626af783594131c97e90e813ad56</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T21:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/egypt-at-least-31-dead-after-fuel-truck-overturns-on-highway/a-80055175--08e39bb25efc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/egypt-at-least-31-dead-after-fuel-truck-overturns-on-highway/a-80055175?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The accident occurred on the packed Ring Road in Giza near Cairo. Dozens of ambulances responded to the crash, and Egyptian health authorities say the death toll could rise.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria detains 5 Mexicans, confiscates over $220 million of meth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:05bc3dd25d1fde512ed001fe26639b537f7de6d08b26211e5931ddbe8709496f</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T20:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-detains-5-mexicans-confiscates-over-220-million-of-meth/a-80054606--ed6de81a9556.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-detains-5-mexicans-confiscates-over-220-million-of-meth/a-80054606?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nigeria's anti-drug agency said Mexican experts were allegedly recruited by a Nigerian national to run a meth laboratory in the southeastern state of Enugu.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
